# ============================================================
#  CHAIN: Ilse Dumont (expansion)
#  Kael's younger sister, raised by the Hollow cult. She takes a room
#  above the bakery in year 2 (hs_ilse_arrives, X11); you meet her
#  there if you follow the lead, or at the gates (hs_kael_sister).
#    ilse_village -> ilse_frost_lessons -> ilse_grey_returns
#      -> (ilse_saved) ilse_kael_reunion / ilse_northern_letter / ilse_farewell
#      -> (ilse_taken) she is gone north
# ============================================================

@event ilse_village
title: The Girl at the Bakery
place: village
class: story
tone: eerie
actor: ilse
when: not met(ilse) and (flag(ilse_in_village) or flag(met_sister))
weight: 20
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: ilse
scene: A village bakery counter, a pale girl in white furs pushing a coin that is visibly frosted across the wood, a baffled baker.
text: In the village bakery a girl in white furs is trying to pay for a bun with a coin so cold it has frozen to the counter. The baker is losing patience. You recognise those eyes: they're Kael's. "Ilse," she says, before you ask. "Don't."
> left: Pay for her bun
  meet ilse
  gold -tiny
  rel ilse +medium
  say: She stares at the bun, then at you, as if kindness is a trick she hasn't learned the counter to yet. "Fine," she says. "Thank you. Fine."
> right: Leave her to it
  meet ilse
  rel ilse -tiny
  say: You leave. Through the window you see the coin crack, and the baker's breath freeze in the air. Ilse walks out with the bun. Nobody stops her.

@event ilse_frost_lessons
title: A Trade in Winter
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: social
actor: ilse
when: rel(ilse) >= 3
weight: 14
art: snow
tags: magic hollowstar
chain: ilse
scene: A frozen pond at the edge of the woods, a girl in white furs drawing a perfect hexagon of frost in the air, a student copying her clumsily.
text: Ilse finds you by the frozen pond. "My brother won't talk to me. You will. Tell me how he really is, and I'll teach you Northern frost-craft. It's better than anything your professors know."
> left: Tell her the truth about Kael
  rel ilse +large
  arcana +medium
  say: You tell her about the cold hands, the roof at three in the morning, the bread. She listens without moving. Then she teaches you to freeze a falling leaf mid-air.
> right: Protect Kael's privacy
  rel ilse -small
  rel kael +small
  say: "He can tell you himself," you say. Ilse's eyes go flat. But the next day, she's at the pond again. "Fine. I'll teach you anyway. You'll need it."

@event ilse_grey_returns
time: night
title: The Man in Grey Comes for Ilse
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: social
actor: ilse
when: rel(ilse) >= 7 and turn >= 20 and not flag(ilse_saved) and not flag(ilse_taken)
weight: 18
art: mask
tags: danger hollowstar
chain: ilse
scene: A moonlit village lane, a man in a grey coat with one hand on a girl's shoulder, frost and shadow coiling around them both.
text: Late at night, a lane behind the bakery. The man in grey has one hand on Ilse's shoulder. "Home," he is saying softly. "Your family is waiting. The door is waiting." Ilse sees you. She doesn't call out. She just looks.
> left: Step between them
  challenge combat trivial:
    win:
      flag ilse_saved
      rel ilse +large
      renown +small
      alignment +small
      find ilse_truth
      say: Your spell breaks his grip. He looks at his frosted hand with mild surprise, bows, and walks into the dark. Ilse is shaking. "Nobody's ever — " she says, and stops.
    lose:
      flag ilse_taken
      health -large
      alignment +small
      find ilse_truth
      say: He swats your spell aside like a moth. When you get up, the lane is empty except for a single white glove in the snow.
> right: Run for Kael
  if met(kael):
    flag ilse_saved
    rel kael +large
    rel ilse +medium
    find ilse_truth
    say: Kael arrives like a blizzard. The man in grey takes one look at him and leaves without a word. Brother and sister stand in the snow, not touching, not speaking.
  else:
    flag ilse_taken
    mood -medium
    find ilse_truth
    say: By the time you're back with help, the lane is empty. There's frost on the cobbles in the shape of a closed door.

@event ilse_kael_reunion
title: Brother and Sister
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: social
actor: ilse
when: flag(ilse_saved) and met(kael) and not flag(dumont_reunited)
weight: 16
art: snow
tags: social hollowstar
chain: ilse
scene: Two pale siblings on opposite ends of a frozen jetty, a third person between them holding three cups of tea.
text: Kael and Ilse have been in the same village for weeks and have spoken eleven words to each other. You have three cups of tea, a frozen jetty and a very bad idea.
> left: Sit them both down
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      flag dumont_reunited
      rel kael +large
      rel ilse +large
      say: It takes an hour and two cups of tea are frozen solid. Then Ilse says "I was scared," and Kael says "So was I," and you quietly leave them to it.
    lose:
      rel kael +small
      rel ilse +small
      say: They argue in a language you don't speak, at a temperature you can't endure. But they argue — which, you suspect, is a start.
> right: Let them find their own way
  rel kael +small
  rel ilse +small
  say: You leave the tea on the jetty. A week later you see them walking by the lake together, a careful arm's length apart. Then less.

@event ilse_northern_letter
title: A Summons From the North
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: social
actor: ilse
when: flag(ilse_saved) and final_year and not flag(ilse_decided)
weight: 14
art: letter
tags: hollowstar
chain: ilse
scene: A girl holding a letter sealed with a black star, standing at a window that looks north toward far white mountains.
text: A letter with a black-star seal. The Dumont family summons Ilse home. "If I don't go, they'll send someone worse than the man in grey," she says. "If I do go, I could tell them to their faces that it's over. Or they could keep me."
> left: "Go. Tell them it's over."
  flag ilse_decided ilse_went_north
  rel ilse +medium
  say: She leaves on the dawn barge, chin up. Before she goes, she presses her forehead to yours, a Northern farewell. "If I'm not back by graduation," she says, "come and get me."
> right: "Stay. Let them come."
  flag ilse_decided
  rel ilse +large
  gain frost_ward
  say: She stays. She sews a sliver of winter into your collar "in case they do come". Nobody does. Not yet.

@event ilse_farewell
title: Snow in Blossomtide
class: story
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: ilse
when: flag(ilse_saved) and final_year and month >= 9 and not flag(ilse_goodbye)
weight: 14
art: snow
tags: social
chain: ilse
scene: A single snowflake falling in a spring orchard full of blossom, a girl in white furs catching it on her glove and holding it out.
text: It's spring, the orchard is in full blossom, and it is snowing — gently, over one tree. Ilse is underneath it. "Graduation's soon," she says. "Everyone's leaving. I wanted to give you something before you forgot me."
> left: "I won't forget you."
  flag ilse_goodbye
  rel ilse +large
  gain frost_ward
  mood +medium
  say: She doesn't believe you, but she smiles anyway — the first real smile you've seen on her. She gives you a snowflake that never melts.
> right: Invite her to the graduation
  flag ilse_goodbye
  rel ilse +large
  rel kael +small
  say: "Me? At a graduation?" She looks horrified, and then, slowly, delighted. On the day, she sits next to Kael in the second row and cries more than anyone.
